<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" standalone="yes"?><rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><channel><title>Lichtspielhaus on Typophile Archive</title><link>https://jolg42.github.io/typophile/tags/lichtspielhaus/</link><description>Recent content in Lichtspielhaus on Typophile Archive</description><generator>Hugo</generator><language>en-us</language><lastBuildDate>Fri, 23 May 2014 01:17:00 +0200</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://jolg42.github.io/typophile/tags/lichtspielhaus/index.xml" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><title>Out Now: LICHTSPIELHAUS. A TYPE NOIR.</title><link>https://jolg42.github.io/typophile/116769/</link><pubDate>Fri, 23 May 2014 01:17:00 +0200</pubDate><guid>https://jolg42.github.io/typophile/116769/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;&amp;ldquo;Lichtspielhaus&amp;rdquo; is a ultra condensed Lichtspiele Spin-Off with 8 weights. It still transports you back to a time where neon lights and marquee letters decorated cinema facades.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;There are 8 styles: Hairline, Thin, Light, Regular, Medium, Bold, Black and Heavy.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;ldquo;Lichtspielhaus&amp;rdquo; is the first part of a new Type Noir Quadrilogy.&lt;/p&gt;
